            <ArticleTitle>Atypical odontalgia. Its aetiology and prognosis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>46-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Atypical odontalgia is a chronic pain disorder in which persistent pain develops in clinically normal teeth. Its possible aetiology and long-term prognosis are discussed. Suggested management regimes are reviewed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
